# Line-ending normalization.
#
# The repository stores all text as LF in the index. Working trees may use the
# platform-native ending (CRLF on Windows) -- that is a checkout-time concern
# only and never reaches a commit. Declaring this here makes normalization a
# property of the repo rather than of each developer's local core.autocrlf,
# so a contributor with autocrlf unset cannot commit CRLF blobs.
#
# Verified no-op at introduction: `git ls-files --eol` reported i/lf for all
# 191 tracked text files, so this codifies existing state and renormalizes
# nothing.
* text=auto

# Source and config -- LF in the index, native in the working tree.
*.js    text
*.json  text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.md    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.toml  text
*.rules text

# Scripts whose ending is load-bearing regardless of platform.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary -- never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
